imageHint: "Toledo Cathedral exterior at night",
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Die Kathedrale Santa María de Toledo, die Primaskathedrale von Spanien, ist eines der großartigsten Meisterwerke der spanischen Gotik. Der Bau begann im Jahr 1226 unter der Herrschaft von Ferdinand III. auf den Fundamenten einer alten Moschee, die wiederum an der Stelle einer westgotischen Kirche stand, und dauerte bis ins späte 15. Jahrhundert. Dieses gigantische Bauwerk mit seinen fünf Schiffen zeichnet sich durch seine unglaubliche Detailfülle aus, darunter der prächtige gotische Hauptaltar aus polychromem Holz und die kunstvolle 'El Transparente' – ein barockes Altarbild, das durch ein meisterhaft in die Decke geschlagenes Fenster himmlisch beleuchtet wird. Die Kathedrale gleicht einem Museum, denn ihre Sakristei beherbergt eine unschätzbare Sammlung von Gemälden weltberühmter Meister, allen voran El Greco ('Die Entkleidung Christi'), aber auch Tizian, Velázquez, Goya und Caravaggio.",
      hu: "A toledói Santa María katedrális, Spanyolország prímási székesegyháza, a spanyol gótikus építészet egyik legnagyszerűbb mesterműve. Az építkezést 1226-ban, III. Ferdinánd uralkodása alatt kezdték meg egy egykori mecset alapjain – amely korábban egy vizigót templom helyén állt –, és a munkálatok egészen a 15. század végéig tartottak. A hatalmas, öthajós építmény lenyűgöző részletgazdagsággal bír. Legszebb elemei közé tartozik a lenyűgöző, színesre festett fából faragott gótikus főoltár, valamint az 'El Transparente' – egy különleges barokk oltár, amelyet a mennyezetbe vágott ablakon át beáramló fény mennyei módon világít meg. A katedrális valóságos művészeti múzeum is egyben: sekrestyéjében világhírű mesterek festményeinek felbecsülhetetlen értékű gyűjteményét őrzik, köztük El Greco ('Krisztus megfosztása ruháitól'), Tiziano, Velázquez, Goya és Caravaggio alkotásait.",
      ro: "Catedrala Santa María din Toledo, catedrala primatială a Spaniei, este una dintre cele mai grandioase capodopere ale arhitecturii gotice spaniole. Construcția a început în 1226 sub domnia lui Ferdinand al III-lea pe fundațiile unei vechi moschei, care la rândul ei se afla pe locul unei biserici vizigote, și a durat până la sfârșitul secolului al XV-lea. Această structură gigantică, cu cele cinci nave ale sale, se distinge prin bogăția incredibilă a detaliilor, inclusiv splendidul altar principal gotic realizat din lemn policrom și ingeniosul 'El Transparente' – un retablu baroc iluminat ceresc printr-o fereastră tăiată cu măiestrie în tavan. Catedrala seamănă cu un muzeu, deoarece sacristia sa găzduiește o colecție neprețuită de picturi ale unor maeștri de renume mondial, în special El Greco ('Dezbrăcarea lui Hristos'), dar și Tițian, Velázquez, Goya și Caravaggio.",
      en: "The Santa Iglesia Catedral Primada de Toledo is widely considered the magnum opus of Spanish Gothic architecture and the spiritual center of Spain. Construction began in 1226 during the reign of Ferdinand III on the footprint of the city's former main mosque, which itself had replaced a Visigothic church. It was not until 1493, during the era of the Catholic Monarchs, that the monumental five-nave building was completed. The cathedral blends French Gothic influences with Moorish Mudéjar elements, particularly visible in the horseshoe arch architecture of the triforium. An absolute highlight of the interior is 'El Transparente', a Baroque masterpiece of alabaster, marble, and bronze, which is dramatically illuminated by heavenly light streaming through a masterfully cut skylight in the vaulted ceiling.",
//       en: "The Cathedral of Santa María of Toledo, the Primate Cathedral of Spain, is one of the most magnificent masterpieces of Spanish Gothic architecture. Construction began in 1226 under the reign of Ferdinand III on the foundations of an old mosque, which in turn stood on the site of a Visigothic church, and continued until the late 15th century. This gigantic five-nave structure is distinguished by its incredible wealth of detail, including the magnificent Gothic high altar made of polychrome wood and the ingenious 'El Transparente'—a Baroque altarpiece illuminated heavenly by a skylight masterfully cut into the vaulted ceiling. The cathedral also serves as an extraordinary art museum; its sacristy houses an invaluable collection of paintings by world-renowned masters, most notably El Greco ('The Disrobing of Christ'), as well as Titian, Velázquez, Goya, and Caravaggio."
    },
